# FreeRADIUS mods-config/files/authorize for radius-admin-chap-hashed-freeradius.
#
# The password is stored HASHED, as {sha256} over the fixture password
# "fixture-chap-secret". The server therefore cannot compute the CHAP digest,
# and RFC 2865 Section 2.2 tells it what to do: "If the password is not
# available in cleartext to the RADIUS server then the server MUST send an
# Access-Reject to the client."
#
# The same entry accepts the same password over PAP. The checker proves that
# with radclient before it reads the rejection, so the rejection cannot be
# explained by a wrong username or a wrong password in this file.
radiusop	Password-With-Header := "{sha256}ar0ZJw9ixbA6LpsWQYWzA/4cmajW11xulQsp2JTJaZM="
		Filter-Id = "interop-operator"
